    <p>Good pest work is partly about denying the bugs a way in, and that overlaps with the upkeep trades a homeowner is already buying. Sealing entry points, fixing torn screens, and closing gaps around the foundation is exactly the punch-list a <a href="/locations/decatur/handyman/">Decatur handyman</a> handles, and a mildew-streaked siding or a damp, debris-packed foundation line — the kind of thing a <a href="/locations/decatur/pressure-washing/">Decatur pressure washing crew</a> clears out — is what gives roaches and ants the moisture and cover they're looking for in the first place. Naming those connections on the page is honest, and it tells Google your site is the hub for how a Decatur homeowner actually keeps a property in shape.</p>

